		{"id":"f948dd9036679f2a","type":"text","text":"\n\n# PPJ BUSINESS ENGLISH SPEAKING & LISTENING\n\n## SESSION 5 WORKSHEET — ASKING FOR CLARIFICATION\n\nLevel: A1–A2 Today’s goal: \nBạn có thể hỏi lại, yêu cầu giải thích, \nxác nhận thông tin \nvà tiếp tục cuộc trò chuyện một cách lịch sự khi chưa hiểu rõ.\n\n1. READING — IT IS OKAY TO ASK AGAIN\n\n# Read the text\n\n### A Clear Question Prevents a Bigger Problem\n\nLinh works in the Import–Export Team. \nOne morning, she receives a call from a supplier. \nThe supplier speaks quickly and gives instructions about a shipment. \nLinh hears the delivery date, but **she does not understand which documents the supplier needs.**\n\nAt first, Linh feels nervous. \nShe does not want the supplier to think that her English is weak. \nHowever, she knows that guessing can create a serious problem.\n\nLinh says, “I’m sorry, I didn’t catch the last part. Could you repeat that more slowly, please?”\n\nThe supplier repeats the in-struction. \nLinh understands that she needs to send the **packing list and the commercial invoice** before three o’clock.\n\nLinh then checks her understanding: \n“Let me make sure I understand correctly. \nYou need the **packing list** and the **commercial invoice** before three p.m., right?”\n\nThe supplier confirms the information.\n\nBecause Linh asks clear and polite questions, she avoids sending the wrong documents. \nShe also shows *re-spon-si-bi-li-ty and pro-fes-sio-na-lism.*\n\n**Asking for cla-ri-fi-ca-tion is not a sign of weakness.** \nIt shows that you care about accuracy. \nWhen information is unclear, it is better to ask again than to make a costly mistake later.\n\nNew Vocabulary \n\n|                  |                       |\n| ---------------- | --------------------- |\n| Word / Phrase    | Meaning in Vietnamese |\n| instruction      | hướng dẫn, chỉ dẫn    |\n| catch            | nghe kịp, hiểu được   |\n| guess            | đoán                  |\n| repeat           | lặp lại               |\n| clarify          | làm rõ                |\n| confirm          | xác nhận              |\n| accuracy         | độ chính xác          |\n| misunderstanding | sự hiểu nhầm          |\n| avoid            | tránh                 |\n\n  \n  \n\n## Multiple-Choice Questions\n\n### 1. Why does Linh feel nervous?\n\nA. She forgot the supplier’s name.\n\nB. She does not understand part of the instruction. \n\nC. She cannot find the documents.\n\nD. She is late for a meeting.\n\n### 2. What does Linh ask the supplier to do?\n\nA. Send an email \n\nB. Change the delivery date \n\nC. Repeat the instruction more slowly \n\nD. Contact Accounting\n\n### 3. Which documents does the supplier need?\n\nA. The PO and delivery note \n\nB. The packing list and commercial invoice \n\nC. The GRN and payment report\n\nD. The shipment report and contract\n\n### 4. When does the supplier need the documents?\n\nA. Before lunch \n\nB. Before two p.m.\n\n C. Before three p.m. \n\nD. Before the end of the week\n\n### 5. What is the main lesson of the reading?\n\nA. You should always speak quickly. \n\nB. You should guess when information is unclear. \n\nC. Asking for cla-ri-fi-ca-tion helps prevent mistakes.  // CLARIFY (VERB)\n\nD. Suppliers should only communicate by email.\n\n# 2. EXPRESSION BANK — ASKING FOR CLARIFICATION\n\n## Function A — You Did Not Hear Clearly\n\n|   |   |   |   |   |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Complete Expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected-Speech Rhythm|PPJ Workplace Example|Rapid-Fire Trigger|\n|Sorry, I didn’t catch that.|Xin lỗi, tôi chưa nghe kịp.|Sorry / I didn’t CATCH that.|The supplier speaks too quickly on the phone.|Không nghe kịp.|\n|Could you repeat that, please?|Bạn có thể lặp lại được không?|Could-you / re-PEAT that / please?|You did not hear the PO number.|Nhờ lặp lại.|\n|Could you say that again, please?|Bạn có thể nói lại được không?|Could-you / say-that-a-GAIN / please?|You missed the delivery date.|Nói lại.|\n|Could you speak a little more slowly, please?|Bạn có thể nói chậm hơn một chút không?|Could-you speak / a-little-more SLOWly / please?|The supplier is speaking too fast.|Nói chậm hơn.|\n\n## Function B — You Heard the Words but Do Not Understand\n\n|   |   |   |   |   |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Complete Expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected-Speech Rhythm|PPJ Workplace Example|Rapid-Fire Trigger|\n|What do you mean by “pending”?|“Pending” có nghĩa là gì?|What-do-you MEAN by / pending?|You do not understand a status word.|Hỏi nghĩa.|\n|Could you explain that again?|Bạn có thể giải thích lại không?|Could-you ex-PLAIN that-a-gain?|The supplier’s process is unclear.|Giải thích lại.|\n|Could you rephrase that, please?|Bạn có thể diễn đạt theo cách khác không?|Could-you re-PHRASE that / please?|You know the words, but not the full meaning.|Nói cách khác.|\n|I’m not sure I understand the instruction.|Tôi chưa chắc mình hiểu hướng dẫn.|I’m-not-SURE / I-understand-the-instruction.|The requested action is unclear.|Chưa hiểu rõ.|\n\n  \n\n## Function C — Ask for More Details\n\n|   |   |   |   |   |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|Complete Expression|Meaning in Vietnamese|Connected-Speech Rhythm|PPJ Workplace Example|Rapid-Fire Trigger|\n|Could you give me an example?|Bạn có thể cho tôi một ví dụ không?|Could-you GIVE me / an-example?|You need an example of the required format.|Xin ví dụ.|\n|Which document do you mean?|Bạn đang nói đến chứng từ nào?|Which DOCument / do-you-mean?|The supplier says “the document.”|Chứng từ nào?|\n|Which quantity should we use?|Chúng ta nên dùng số lượng nào?|Which QUANtity / should-we-use?|The invoice and PO show different quantities.|Số lượng nào?|\n|When exactly do you need it?|Chính xác bạn cần khi nào?|When-exactly / do-you NEED it?|The deadline is unclear.|Deadline chính xác?|\n\n  \n\n## Function D — Check Your Understanding\n\n|                                                   |                                                      |                                               |                                        |                     |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| Complete Expression                               | Meaning in Vietnamese                                | Connected-Speech Rhythm                       | PPJ Workplace Example                  | Rapid-Fire Trigger  |\n| Let me make sure I understand correctly.          | Để tôi chắc rằng mình hiểu đúng.                     | Let-me-make-SURE / I-understand-correctly.    | Before you repeat the instruction.     | Kiểm tra hiểu đúng. |\n| So, you need the **packing list** *today*, right? | Vậy bạn cần packing list hôm nay, đúng không?        | So-you-NEED / the-packing-list-today / right? | Confirm the document and deadline.     | Xác nhận lại.       |\n| Do you mean we should update the PO first?        | Ý bạn là chúng tôi nên cập nhật PO trước đúng không? | Do-you-MEAN / we-should-update-the-PO-first?  | Confirm the sequence of actions.       | Ý bạn là…?          |\n| Just to confirm, the deadline is ... three p.m.   | Xin xác nhận, deadline là ba giờ chiều.              | Just-to-con-FIRM / the-deadline-is-three-p.m. | Confirm a time before ending the call. | Xác nhận deadline.  |\n\n  \n\n## Function E — Respond and Continue\n\n|                                                           |                                           |                                               |                                          |                    |\n| --------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------ |\n| Complete Expression                                       | Meaning in Vietnamese                     | Connected-Speech Rhythm                       | PPJ Workplace Example                    | Rapid-Fire Trigger |\n| Okay, I understand now.                                   | Được rồi, giờ tôi hiểu rồi.               | Okay / I-under-STAND now.                     | The supplier has explained again.        | Đã hiểu.           |\n| Thank you for + (NOUN) :: VERB_ING / S / clarifying that. | Cảm ơn bạn đã làm rõ.                     | Thank-you-for CLARifying-that.                | Close the clarification politely.        | Cảm ơn làm rõ.     |\n| Let me write that down.                                   | Để tôi ghi lại.                           | Let-me-WRITE that-down.                       | You need to record a number or deadline. | Ghi lại.           |\n| I’ll check the details and get back to you.               | Tôi sẽ kiểm tra chi tiết và phản hồi lại. | I’ll-CHECK the-details / and-get-back-to-you. | You need internal confirmation first.    | Cần kiểm tra thêm. |\n\n  \n\n# 3. SPEAKING PATTERNS\n\n## Pattern 1 — Ask Someone to Repeat\n\n### Framework\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch __________________.\n\n  \n\nCould you repeat __________________, please?\n\n### Sample Answer\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch the PO number. Could you repeat it, please?\n\n### Your Turn\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch ______________________________. Could you repeat ______________________________, please?\n\n  \n\n## Pattern 2 — Ask for a Clearer Explanation\n\n### Framework\n\nI’m not sure I understand __________________.\n\n  \n\nCould you explain __________________ again?\n\n### Sample Answer\n\nI’m not sure I understand the new delivery process. Could you explain the second step again?\n\n### Your Turn\n\nI’m not sure I understand ______________________________. Could you explain ______________________________ again?\n\n  \n\n## Pattern 3 — Ask for Specific Details\n\n### Framework\n\nWhich __________________ do you mean?\n\n  \n\nWhen exactly do you need __________________?\n\n### Sample Answer\n\nWhich invoice do you mean? When exactly do you need the corrected file?\n\n### Your Turn\n\nWhich ______________________________ do you mean? When exactly do you need ______________________________?\n\n  \n\n## Pattern 4 — Confirm Your Understanding\n\n### Framework\n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly.\n\n  \n\nYou need __________________ before __________________, right?\n\n### Sample Answer\n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly. You need the packing list before three p.m., right?\n\n### Your Turn\n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly. You need ______________________________ before ______________________________, right?\n\n  \n\n## Pattern 5 — Clarify, Confirm and Close\n\n### Framework\n\nSorry, I didn’t understand __________________.\n\n  \n\nCould you clarify __________________?\n\n  \n\nSo, I need to __________________, correct?\n\n  \n\nThank you for clarifying that.\n\n### Sample Answer\n\nSorry, I didn’t understand the final instruction. Could you clarify which quantity I should enter? So, I need to use the actual received quantity, correct? Thank you for clarifying that.\n\n### Your Turn\n\nSorry, I didn’t understand ______________________________. Could you clarify ______________________________? So, I need to ______________________________, correct? Thank you for clarifying that.\n\n  \n\n# 4. THE CLARIFICATION LADDER\n\nKhi bạn chưa hiểu, đừng dừng lại ở:\n\nWhat?\n\nHãy đi từng bước.\n\n## Step 1 — Signal the Problem\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch the last part.\n\n## Step 2 — Ask for Repetition\n\nCould you repeat that more slowly, please?\n\n## Step 3 — Identify the Unclear Detail\n\nWhich document do you mean?\n\n## Step 4 — Ask for an Example or Explanation\n\nCould you give me an example of the correct format?\n\n## Step 5 — Confirm Your Understanding\n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly.\n\nYou need the revised packing list before three p.m., right?\n\n## Step 6 — Confirm the Next Action\n\nOkay. I’ll revise the packing list and send it before three p.m.\n\n## Step 7 — Close Politely\n\nThank you for clarifying that.\n\n  \n\n## Complete Clarification Ladder Example\n\n### Supplier’s Unclear Instruction\n\nPlease correct the file and send the final version before the shipment is processed.\n\n### Your Response\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch the last part.\n\n  \n\nCould you repeat that more slowly, please?\n\n  \n\nWhich file do you mean?\n\n  \n\nCould you explain what needs to be corrected?\n\n  \n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly.\n\n  \n\nYou need us to correct the packing list and send the final version before three p.m., right?\n\n  \n\nOkay. I’ll check the quantity, revise the packing list and send it before three p.m.\n\n  \n\nThank you for clarifying that.\n\n  \n\n# 5. PRONUNCIATION — POLITE INTONATION\n\n## A. Direct Voice vs Polite Voice\n\nA polite clarification question usually has:\n\n- a calm beginning;\n    \n- stress on the important word;\n    \n- a gentle rise at the end;\n    \n- no angry or sudden tone.\n    \n\n  \n\n## Practice 1 — Gentle Rising Intonation ↑\n\nRead with a gentle rise.\n\nCould you repeat that, please? ↑\n\n  \n\nCould you say that again, please? ↑\n\n  \n\nCould you speak more slowly, please? ↑\n\n  \n\nCould you give me an example? ↑\n\nDo not say the sentence too sharply:\n\nRepeat that. ↓\n\nUse:\n\nCould you repeat that, please? ↑\n\n  \n\n## Practice 2 — Stress the Key Word\n\nCould you rePEAT that, please? ↑\n\n  \n\nCould you speak more SLOWly, please? ↑\n\n  \n\nWhich DOCument do you mean? ↑\n\n  \n\nWhen EXactly do you need it? ↑\n\n  \n\nCould you give me an EXample? ↑\n\n  \n\n## Practice 3 — Falling Intonation for Confirmation ↓\n\nUse a calm falling tone when you summarize confidently.\n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly. ↓\n\n  \n\nYou need the packing list before three p.m., right? ↑\n\n  \n\nOkay, I understand now. ↓\n\n  \n\nThank you for clarifying that. ↓\n\n  \n\n## Rhythm Drill\n\nClap once on the stressed word.\n\nCould-you re-PEAT that / please?\n\n  \n\nCould-you speak / more SLOWly / please?\n\n  \n\nWhich DOCument / do-you-mean?\n\n  \n\nWhen EXactly / do-you-need-it?\n\n  \n\nLet-me-make-SURE / I-understand-correctly.\n\n  \n\n## Partner Drill\n\n### Partner A says the trigger:\n\nKhông nghe kịp.\n\n### Partner B responds:\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch that. Could you repeat it, please?\n\nContinue with:\n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Trigger|Response|\n|Không hiểu nghĩa|What do you mean by that?|\n|Cần ví dụ|Could you give me an example?|\n|Không rõ chứng từ|Which document do you mean?|\n|Không rõ deadline|When exactly do you need it?|\n|Muốn xác nhận|Let me make sure I understand correctly.|\n\n  \n\n# 6. ROLEPLAY — UNCLEAR SUPPLIER INSTRUCTIONS\n\n## Situation\n\nBạn đang trao đổi với một supplier về một lô hàng. Supplier đưa ra hướng dẫn chưa rõ ràng.\n\nBạn không được đoán.\n\nBạn phải sử dụng Clarification Ladder để hiểu chính xác:\n\n- document;\n    \n- quantity;\n    \n- deadline;\n    \n- next action.\n    \n\n## Role A — Supplier\n\nYour information:\n\nThe shipment is planned for Friday.\n\n  \n\nThe packing list shows 500 pieces.\n\n  \n\nThe actual quantity is 480 pieces.\n\n  \n\nYou need PPJ to revise the packing list.\n\n  \n\nYou need the revised document before 3:00 p.m. today.\n\n  \n\nAfter receiving it, you will send a confirmation email.\n\n### Begin with an unclear instruction\n\nPlease correct the document and send it soon because we need it for the shipment.\n\nDo not give all the information immediately.\n\nOnly answer when your partner asks clear questions.\n\n## Role B — PPJ Employee\n\nYou hear:\n\nPlease correct the document and send it soon because we need it for the shipment.\n\nYou need to clarify:\n\n1. Which document?\n    \n2. What information is incorrect?\n    \n3. Which quantity is correct?\n    \n4. What is the exact deadline?\n    \n5. What will the supplier do next?\n    \n\n### Use at least six expressions\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch the last part.\n\n  \n\nCould you repeat that more slowly, please?\n\n  \n\nWhich document do you mean?\n\n  \n\nWhich quantity should we use?\n\n  \n\nWhen exactly do you need it?\n\n  \n\nCould you explain what needs to be corrected?\n\n  \n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly.\n\n  \n\nSo, we should use 480 pieces, right?\n\n  \n\nThank you for clarifying that.\n\n  \n\n## Your Final Summary\n\nComplete before ending the conversation:\n\nLet me summarize the instruction.\n\n  \n\nWe need to revise the __________________________.\n\n  \n\nThe correct quantity is __________________ pieces.\n\n  \n\nWe need to send it before ______________________.\n\n  \n\nAfter that, the supplier will ___________________.\n\n  \n\nIs that correct?\n\n  \n\n## Roleplay Challenge\n\nAfter Round 1, change roles.\n\nIn Round 2, add one new unclear detail:\n\nThe invoice number is unclear.\n\n  \n\nThe delivery date has changed.\n\n  \n\nThe supplier mentions two different deadlines.\n\n  \n\nThe requested file format is unclear.\n\n  \n\nThe supplier uses the words “the final document” without naming it.\n\n  \n\n## Success Check\n\n□ I asked the supplier to repeat information.\n\n  \n\n□ I asked about one specific unclear detail.\n\n  \n\n□ I asked for an exact deadline.\n\n  \n\n□ I confirmed the correct quantity.\n\n  \n\n□ I summarized the next action.\n\n  \n\n□ I closed the conversation politely.\n\n  \n  \n\n# SESSION 5 TAKEAWAY\n\nBạn không cần giả vờ hiểu.\n\nBạn có thể nói:\n\nSorry, I didn’t catch that.\n\n  \n\nCould you repeat that, please?\n\n  \n\nWhat do you mean by that?\n\n  \n\nCould you give me an example?\n\n  \n\nLet me make sure I understand correctly.\n\n  \n\nThank you for clarifying that.\n\nClear questions prevent costly mistakes.\n\n  \n  \n**","x":3040,"y":-1280,"width":980,"height":13706,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"31c7b0b7a77e15f0","type":"text","text":"could you **describe your morning** ? --- // shouldnt be used\n\n-> could you share with me how was your morning ?\n\n-> how was your morning, anything good?\n\n\n\n","x":-2760,"y":1143,"width":380,"height":320,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e82ecdbc2d6b218f","type":"text","text":"CONTACTED the invoices service provider \n-> to fix some data mistakes \n-> request a report \n-> send a message to my boss to schedule a bio-metric verification for my company account","x":-2360,"y":923,"width":380,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"1be102effa7fb81b","type":"text","text":"\n\n# 20 cụm từ/câu A1–A2 cho bài: Daily Habits & Workload\n\nDựa trên theme Chapter 6: Exploring Daily Habits — routine, schedule, daily habits, last-minute tasks, postponed tasks — mình chuyển thành ngôn ngữ workplace đơn giản để học viên mô tả một ngày làm việc bình thường tại PPJ.\n\n|     |                                  |                                      |                                 |                                                               |\n| --- | -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| #   | Expression                       | Meaning                              | Rhythm / Pronunciation          | PPJ Context / Example                                         |\n| 1   | I start work at 8.               | Tôi bắt đầu làm lúc 8 giờ.           | I START work at EIGHT           | I start work at 8. Then I check my messages.                  |\n| 2   | I usually check my email first.  | Tôi thường kiểm tra email trước.     | I USually check my Email first  | Accounting / XNK / Purchasing: kiểm tra email đầu ngày.       |\n| 3   | First, I check my tasks.         | Đầu tiên, tôi kiểm tra công việc.    | FIRST, I check my TASKS         | ==Dùng để bắt đầu mô tả routine.==                            |\n| 4   | Then I update the file.          | Sau đó tôi cập nhật file.            | THEN I update the FILE          | Cập nhật Excel, report, tracking sheet.                       |\n| 5   | After that, I call the supplier. | Sau đó tôi gọi supplier.             | AFter that, I CALL the supplier | Purchasing / Sourcing follow-up supplier.                     |\n| 6   | I have a lot to do today.        | Hôm nay tôi có nhiều việc phải làm.  | I have-a LOT to DO today        | Dùng khi workload cao nhưng vẫn đơn giản.                     |\n| 7   | It’s a busy day.                 | Hôm nay bận.                         | It’s-a BUSY day                 | Phiên bản A1 của “It’s been a busy morning.”                  |\n| 8   | This is urgent.                  | Việc này gấp.                        | THIS is URgent                  | Khi có PO, invoice, shipment, material issue cần xử lý nhanh. |\n| 9   | This is my priority.             | Đây là ưu tiên của tôi.              | This is my priORity             | Nói task quan trọng nhất trong ngày.                          |\n| 10  | I need to finish this today.     | Tôi cần hoàn thành việc này hôm nay. | I NEED to FINish this today     | Deadline trong ngày.                                          |\n| 11  | I still need to check it.        | Tôi vẫn cần kiểm tra việc đó.        | I STILL need to CHECK it        | Khi chưa thể xác nhận thông tin.                              |\n| 12  | I still need to send the report. | Tôi vẫn cần gửi báo cáo.             | I STILL need to SEND the rePORT | Dùng cho Finance, Warehouse, QC, Production report.           |\n| 13  | I’m working on it now.           | Tôi đang làm việc đó.                | I’m WORKing on-it NOW           | Khi người khác hỏi tiến độ.                                   |\n| 14  | I’m tied up with invoices.       | Tôi đang bận xử lý invoices.         | I’m TIED up with INvoices       | A2; có thể thay noun: documents, emails, reports, stock data. |\n| 15  | I have one task pending.         | Tôi còn một việc đang chờ xử lý.     | I have ONE task PENDing         | Phiên bản đơn giản của “I’ve got a few things pending.”       |\n| 16  | I have some pending tasks.       | Tôi có vài việc đang pending.        | I have SOME PENDing TASKS       | Dùng khi báo workload ngắn gọn.                               |\n| 17  | I need more time.                | Tôi cần thêm thời gian.              | I NEED more TIME                | Khi chưa xong task.                                           |\n| 18  | Can I send it later?             | Tôi gửi sau được không?              | Can I SEND it LAter?            | Hỏi nhẹ khi chưa thể gửi ngay.                                |\n| 19  | I will send it before lunch.     | Tôi sẽ gửi trước giờ ăn trưa.        | I’ll SEND it before LUNCH       | Cam kết thời gian đơn giản.                                   |\n| 20  | I finish work at 5.              | Tôi kết thúc công việc lúc 5 giờ.    | I FINish work at FIVE           | Dùng để mô tả full workday routine.                           |\n\n# 10 mẫu Pattern + Sample A1–A2: Talking About My Workday\n\n## Pattern 1 — Normal Workday\n\nPattern\n\nI start work at [time]. First, I check my [email/tasks/messages]. Then I [do my main task]. Today is a [normal/busy/quiet] day. I need to [finish/check/send] [something]. I will finish it by [time].\n\nSample\n\nI start work at 8. \nFirst, I check my email. \nThen I update the report. \nToday is a normal day. \nI need to finish the report. \nI will finish it by 4.\n\n## Pattern 2 — Busy Morning\n\nPattern\n\nIt’s been a busy morning. I have many [tasks/emails/documents] to check. First, I [check/update/prepare] [something]. Then I need to [call/send/confirm] [something]. My priority is [task]. I hope to finish it before [time].\n\nSample\n\nIt’s been a busy morning. \nI have many emails to check. \nFirst, I check the documents. \nThen I need to send the invoice. \nMy priority is the invoice. \nI hope to finish it before lunch.\n\n## Pattern 3 — Pending Tasks\n\nPattern\n\nI have a few things pending. I still need to [check/send/update] [something]. I’m waiting for [person/department/supplier]. After that, I can [finish/confirm/send] it. I will update you by [time].\n\nSample\n\nI have a few things pending. \nI still need to check the invoice. \nI’m waiting for Accounting. \nAfter that, I can confirm it. \nI will update you by 3.\n\n## Pattern 4 — Urgent Task\n\nPattern\n\nToday, I have an urgent task. I need to [finish/check/send/confirm] [something]. This is my priority now. I’m working on it. I will send an update by [time].\n\nSample\n\nToday, I have an urgent task. \nI need to confirm the shipment. This is my priority now. \nI’m working on it. \nI will send an update by 2.\n\n## Pattern 5 — Asking for More Time\n\nPattern\n\nI’m working on [task]. I still need more time. I need to [check/confirm/update] [something] first. Can I send it by [time]? I will update you when it’s done.\n\nSample\n\nI’m working on the report. \nI still need more time. \nI need to check the data first. \nCan I send it by 5? \nI will update you when it’s done.\n\n## Pattern 6 — Working with Another Department\n\nPattern\n\nToday, I need to work with [department]. We need to check [task/document/data]. First, I will [send/call/confirm] [something]. Then we will [check/update/finish] it together. I will follow up later.\n\nSample\n\nToday, I need to work with Warehouse. We need to check the stock data. First, I will send the file. Then we will check it together. I will follow up later.\n\n## Pattern 7 — Supplier Follow-up\n\nPattern\n\nThis morning, I need to follow up with [supplier/customer]. I’m waiting for [confirmation/update/document]. I will send them a message. After they reply, I can [update/confirm/finish] [task]. I’ll keep you posted.\n\nSample\n\nThis morning, I need to follow up with the supplier. I’m waiting for confirmation. I will send them a message. After they reply, I can update the file. I’ll keep you posted.\n\n## Pattern 8 — Problem at Work\n\nPattern\n\nToday, we have a small problem. There is an issue with [invoice/stock/file/shipment]. I need to check it first. Then I will tell [person/department]. I hope we can fix it today.\n\nSample\n\nToday, we have a small problem. There is an issue with the invoice. I need to check it first. Then I will tell Accounting. I hope we can fix it today.\n\n## Pattern 9 — End-of-Day Update\n\nPattern\n\nToday was a [busy/normal/good] day. I finished [task]. I also checked [document/file/data]. I still have [one task/a few things] pending. Tomorrow, I will continue with [task].\n\nSample\n\nToday was a busy day. I finished the report. I also checked the invoice. I still have one task pending. Tomorrow, I will continue with the shipment file.\n\n## Pattern 10 — Simple Daily Routine\n\nPattern\n\nEvery morning, I [check/open/update] [something]. After that, I [send/prepare/review] [something]. In the afternoon, I usually [call/check/follow up]. Before I finish work, I [send/update/confirm] [something]. That is my normal workday.\n\nSample\n\nEvery morning, I check my email. After that, I update the file. In the afternoon, I usually follow up with the supplier. Before I finish work, I send the report. That is my normal workday.\n\nQuick Replacement Bank \n\n|   |   |\n|---|---|\n|Slot|Choices|\n|[time]|8 / 8:30 / 9 / before lunch / by 3 / by 5|\n|[task]|report / invoice / shipment / stock data / email / document / file|\n|[action]|check / send / update / confirm / call / prepare / finish / review|\n|[department]|Accounting / Warehouse / Purchasing / IT / QC / Production / Merchandising|\n|[status]|busy / normal / quiet / urgent / pending / done|\n|[person]|my manager / my team / the supplier / the customer / another department|\n\n  \n  \n**","x":-4280,"y":1013,"width":1380,"height":9121},
